From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:51:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/116] usb: dwc3: qcom: Reapply UTMI pipe clk on resume

The qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk property is used on boards whose
controller has no SuperSpeed PHY, and therefore no PIPE clock: the
glue programs the QSCRATCH GENERAL_CFG register so that the core's
PIPE clock domain runs from the UTMI clock instead. This is done once,
at probe.

When the controller's power domain is collapsed during system suspend,
which happens as soon as unused power domains are no longer kept on,
the QSCRATCH registers lose their contents. On resume the core is
reinitialized with its PIPE domain unclocked, and the gadget fails to
restart:

  dwc3-qcom a600000.usb: failed to enable ep0out

and the USB link stays down until the driver is rebound.

Remember the property at probe and select the UTMI clock again in
dwc3_qcom_resume(), after the clocks and interconnect paths are
enabled and before the core resumes. Tested on SM7250 (USB 2.0 only
port, peripheral mode): the gadget reconnects after s2idle.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg

Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ac68b4218..9e7d2307a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@ struct dwc3_qcom {
 	enum usb_dr_mode	mode;
 	bool			is_suspended;
 	bool			pm_suspended;
+	bool			utmi_as_pipe_clk;
 	struct icc_path		*icc_path_ddr;
 	struct icc_path		*icc_path_apps;
 
@@ -369,6 +370,8 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_suspend(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom);
+
 static int dwc3_qcom_resume(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -388,6 +391,15 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_resume(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 	if (ret)
 		dev_warn(qcom->dev, "failed to enable interconnect: %d\n", ret);
 
+	/*
+	 * The QSCRATCH registers lose their state when the controller's power
+	 * domain is collapsed during system suspend: select the UTMI clock
+	 * for the PIPE domain again, or the core can't run without a PIPE
+	 * clock ("failed to enable ep0out").
+	 */
+	if (qcom->utmi_as_pipe_clk)
+		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
+
 	/* Clear existing events from PHY related to L2 in/out */
 	for (i = 0; i < qcom->num_ports; i++) {
 		dwc3_qcom_setbits(qcom->qscratch_base,
@@ -680,6 +692,7 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 */
 	ignore_pipe_clk = device_property_read_bool(dev,
 				"qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk");
+	qcom->utmi_as_pipe_clk = ignore_pipe_clk;
 	if (ignore_pipe_clk)
 		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);
 
